## Discord account requests (2026-09-20)

The owner authorized exact-username requests followed by verified-recipient, one-use Discord DMs.
Follow [the account contract](../../docs/workspaces-prd.md#discord-account-requests-2026-09-20).
This narrow exception permits only the public signup link in that recipient's DM.
Never disclose private prefixes, reusable login links, passwords, or signup tokens in channel posts.
Create only normal accounts with membership in `vibecoders-ai-generation`.
Never infer account ownership from a matching site name or restore revoked accounts or removed memberships.
Keep the original controller as the sole writer of global accounts, memberships, and signup tickets.
Deploy compatible code to the original and explicitly selected Vibecoders instance before enabling Discord account requests.
Do not roll either instance back to a parser that rejects the new shared account or environment fields.
The feature starts disabled and uses the existing public proxy route.

